# Installation instructions for Get Newick Info

## Prerequisites

Requires a C99 compiler, the math library, and Make or another supported build
tool.

## Autoconf and Automake

Requires Autoconf 2.71 or later and Automake. From the project root:

    ./autogen.sh && ./configure && make

The executable is `./get_newick_info`. Install it to the default `/usr/local`
prefix with `make install`, or set another prefix before building:

    ./configure --prefix="$HOME/.local"
    make
    make install

Use `make uninstall` to remove the installed executable and `make clean` to
remove build products. Use `./configure --bindir=PATH` to select a different
binary directory. For staged installs, set `DESTDIR` consistently for
both `make install` and `make uninstall`. `make check` currently runs no tests.

## CMake

Requires CMake 3.10 or later. From the project root:

    mkdir -p build
    (cd build && cmake ..)
    cmake --build build

Run the CMake smoke test without Python:

    (cd build && ctest --output-on-failure)

Install the executable (the default prefix is usually `/usr/local`):

    cmake --build build --target install

To install into a different prefix, set it when configuring:

    (cd build && cmake .. -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$HOME/.local")
    cmake --build build
    cmake --build build --target install

The executable is `build/get_newick_info`. Use
`cmake --build build --target uninstall` to remove files listed in the install
manifest and `cmake --build build --target clean` to remove build products.
Set `CMAKE_INSTALL_BINDIR` when configuring to select a different binary
directory.
For staged installs, set `DESTDIR` consistently for both the install and
uninstall commands.
